# **2. The Siril sentence matches the source and the documentation**
# - The new text says Siril "keeps only the pixels whose residual lies within med − 4σ to med + 2σ (σ = 1.4826 × MAD) and outside protected bright structure, fits again on those, and stops when the kept set settles".
# - In `siril-bkg.c`:
#   - `AG_HIGH_K 2.0f` and `AG_LOW_K 4.0f`.
#   - `ag_mad_sigma` sets σ = 1.4826 × MAD, taken over the pixels currently kept.
#   - The keep rule is `residual <= med + 2σ && residual >= med − 4σ`, and then `smask` removes the structure mask.
#   - `ag_structure_mask` flags `residual − med > protect_threshold`. That is bright structure only, so "bright" is right.
#   - The fit runs again on `new_keep` and stops when the change is below 1e-4, or after 20 iterations.
